        "original_id": "03635a46-5e81-5682-846a-04233c426168",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Prince Ioann Konstantinovich of Russia; Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia; Yelizaveta Mavrikievna; Emperor Nicholas I of Russia\n- Roles: Russian prince; grand duke; poet; playwright\n\nFacts:\n- Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia was born on 22 August 1858 in Strelna.\n- Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia was a grandson of Emperor Nicholas I of Russia.\n- Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia was a poet and playwright of some renown.\n- Prince Ioann Konstantinovich of Russia was born on 5 July 1886.\n- Prince Ioann Konstantinovich of Russia was the eldest son of Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia and Yelizaveta Mavrikievna, who was born Princess Elisabeth of Saxe-Altenburg.\n- Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich of Russia died on 15 June 1915 in Pavlovsk.\n- Prince Ioann Konstantinovich of Russia, also known as Prince John, Prince Ivan, or Prince Johan, died on 18 July 1918.",
